new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e077f58
--- /dev/null
+++ b/SECURITY.md
@@ -0,0 +1,74 @@
+# Security notes: The Daily Grind website
+
+## Audit summary (2026-10-28)
+
+| # | Finding | Severity | Status |
+|---|---------|----------|--------|
+| 1 | No security response headers (CSP, X-Content-Type-Options, X-Frame-Options, Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy, COOP, CORP, HSTS) | High | Fixed: `security-headers.js`, applied to every response in `server.js` |
+| 2 | `/logout` changed state on a plain GET and was linked as `<a href>`; any third-party page could log a visitor out (logout CSRF) | Medium | Fixed: POST form in the page, GET shows a confirmation page, POST checks `Sec-Fetch-Site`/`Origin`, response carries `Clear-Site-Data` |
+| 3 | Inline `<style>` block and a `style=""` attribute would force `style-src 'unsafe-inline'` | Medium (blocks CSP) | Fixed: CSS moved to `public/styles.css`, attribute replaced with a class |
+| 4 | `new URL(req.url, "http://" + Host)` was unguarded; a malformed `Host` header throws and crashed the process (single-request DoS) | Medium | Fixed: 400 response |
+| 5 | Unsupported methods (POST/PUT/DELETE to any path) were answered 200 with the home page | Low | Fixed: 405 with `Allow` |
+| 6 | Hero image loaded from `images.unsplash.com` (third-party dependency, no integrity possible for images) | Info | Accepted; origin pinned in CSP `img-src`. Self-host to remove the dependency entirely |
+| 7 | No client-side JavaScript present | Info | Policy denies scripts outright; `test/markup.test.js` fails if any `<script>`, `on*=` or `javascript:` is added |
+
+## Headers sent
+
+```
+Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'self';
+  frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; img-src 'self' https://images.unsplash.com;
+  style-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; report-to csp-endpoint; report-uri /csp-report
+Reporting-Endpoints: csp-endpoint="/csp-report"
+X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
+X-Frame-Options: DENY
+X-XSS-Protection: 0
+Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
+Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), geolocation=(), ... (all denied)
+Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
+Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
+Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains   (HTTPS requests only)
+```
+
+Over HTTPS the CSP additionally includes `upgrade-insecure-requests`.
+
+## Safe CSP rollout
+
+The policy ships in **report-only** mode by default. Browsers evaluate it and POST violation
+reports to `/csp-report`, which the server logs as one JSON line per report
+(`{"type":"csp-report", ...}`), but nothing is blocked.
+
+1. Deploy with the default (`CSP_MODE` unset or `report-only`).
+2. Watch logs for `"type":"csp-report"` lines for at least one full traffic cycle. Expect noise
+   from browser extensions; look for repeated `blocked-uri` values that are first-party or that
+   many users hit.
+3. Fix real violations by changing the page or by adding a specific origin to
+   `security-headers.js` (never `'unsafe-inline'`, `*`, or `data:`).
+4. Switch to `CSP_MODE=enforce`. Keep the report endpoint; enforced violations are reported too.
+5. If something breaks in production, `CSP_MODE=report-only` (or `off`) is an instant rollback
+   with no code change.
+
+## Configuration
+
+| Variable | Default | Meaning |
+|----------|---------|---------|
+| `CSP_MODE` | `report-only` | `report-only`, `enforce`, or `off`. Invalid values abort startup. |
+| `TRUST_PROXY` | unset | Set to `1` only when a TLS-terminating proxy sets `X-Forwarded-Proto`; enables HSTS and `upgrade-insecure-requests` for those requests. |
+| `PORT` | `11222` | Listening port. |
+
+## Guard rails for future edits
+
+* `npm test` runs without starting the server. It checks the header policy and lints
+  `index.html` / `public/styles.css` for anything the CSP would block: inline styles or
+  scripts, event-handler attributes, `javascript:` URLs, `<base>`, embeds, `@import`, and
+  remote CSS URLs whose origin is not in `IMAGE_ORIGINS`.
+* Add new stylesheets or images by listing them in `STATIC_FILES` (server) and, for remote
+  origins, `IMAGE_ORIGINS` (policy). Do not add a catch-all static handler.
+* If JavaScript is ever needed, serve it from `/` and add `script-src 'self'` (or nonces).
+  Do not add `'unsafe-inline'`.
+
+## Not covered here
+
+* Real authentication/session handling and a CSRF token: the `Origin`/`Sec-Fetch-Site`
+  check is a baseline for a site with no sessions.
+* Rate limiting on `/csp-report` (it is size-capped at 64 KB per request only).
+* HSTS `preload`: only add once every subdomain is confirmed HTTPS-only.
